# The cheap canonical sample: one or two files per engine family, ~16 files. This
# is what `dev/sample.sh seed` (and therefore `bringup`) puts in a worktree's
# catalog/ -- symlink first, then hardlink, then "unavailable" -- so a new tree has
# something real to browse, play and *test* with, with no network and no copying of
# a large collection.
#
# It deliberately includes the fixtures the dev harnesses reference (TECHTRIS.MOD
# for XMP, 16 Hurry Up!.vgz for VGM loops, G2MST6.MDX for MDX, apollo for V2M,
# tempo_stress for MIDI), so a seeded worktree is also a testable one.
#
# NOT here, on purpose: the big hand-curated collections under catalog/ (1.5 GB on
# this machine). They belong to the branch that curated them; a worktree that wants
# one takes it deliberately with `dev/sample.sh steal <worktree>`.
#
# Paths are relative to the repo root. A PSF-family entry needs its companion
# (`.usflib` / `.gsflib`) listed too -- they are not indexed, but must sit beside
# the song file or it cannot load.
catalog/test.nsf
catalog/nsfe/Navy Blue.nsfe
catalog/spc/01 NFL Theme.spc
catalog/sid/Delta.sid
catalog/gbs/DMG-TRA-0.gbs
catalog/ay/Arkanoid.AY
catalog/arcade-capcom/Ghosts'N_Goblins_(Arcade)/16 Hurry Up!.vgz
catalog/mods/TECHTRIS.MOD
catalog/midi/tempo_stress/1_basic.mid
catalog/midi/tempo_stress/2_markers.mid
catalog/mdx/G2MST6.MDX
catalog/n64/Blast Corps/01 Blast Corps.miniusf
catalog/n64/Blast Corps/NUS-NBCE-USA.usflib
catalog/gsf/Mr. Driller A - Fushigi na Pacteria (2002-08-23)(-)(Namco)[GBA]/18 Epilogue.minigsf
catalog/gsf/Mr. Driller A - Fushigi na Pacteria (2002-08-23)(-)(Namco)[GBA]/AGB-AD5J-JPN.gsflib
catalog/v2m/apollo dvd copy 4.5.4kg.v2m
